From b31e2b2e6096a29bd453e8644a59c14d7b45c479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redactorator build <build@redactorator.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:32:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add content filter options for redaction

Three save options for cleaning a file before redaction. Each runs the
sanitize filter over every page and annotation, as "sanitize" does.

drop-hidden-oc: content inside optional content that is off, as for
viewing, is not written. The sanitize processor sets its usage to
"View", so the interpreter tracks hidden content with the same test
that drawing uses (pdf_is_ocg_hidden), and skips XObjects whose own /OC
is off. Hidden paths, text, images, shadings, forms and marked content
are dropped; hidden text is removed the way redaction removes it, so
the text after it keeps its place; a hidden clipping path still clips,
as when drawing. The optional content markers are removed from content
that stays: BDC /OC and its EMC, and /OC in shown XObjects and
shadings.

drop-mc-properties: a BDC whose properties are not an optional content
group or membership dictionary is written as a BMC with the same tag,
and a DP as an MP. This removes ActualText, Alt, E and any other data
held in marked-content properties.

blank-unshown-pixels: image pixels that no placement shows are blanked,
the same way image redaction blanks them. Before filtering, a device
pass over every page, its annotations and its widgets, as for viewing
and as for printing, records each image placement and the clips in
force there. Each image's shown area
is then drawn in its own pixels: the page bounds under every clip,
unioned over all placements and widened by one pixel. An image XObject
with pixels left over is rewritten in place, so all its uses still
share one object; an image whose pixels are all shown is left as it
was. Inline images are blanked as the filter meets them. Images drawn
inside a tiling pattern are treated as fully shown. An image XObject
that cannot be loaded fails the save, since it cannot be blanked.

The pixel preparation and blanking in pdf_redact_image_imp move into
helpers that both use; redaction behaves as before.

Also fix how an optional content membership dictionary combines its
groups. /P /AllOn counted as on whenever any group was on, and
/P /AnyOff as off whatever the groups were. Each policy now tests
every group, as the PDF specification defines it, and a dictionary
with no groups has no effect. This changes what is drawn as well as
what drop-hidden-oc drops.
